// midterm.js — the Midterm prep question bank, rendered by /midterm (interactive,
// filterable). Data-driven: add a question = append one object to `questions`.
// EN canonical + RU; TT falls back tt → ru → en (this module is NOT scanned by the
// i18n-coverage gate, so en+ru is the model — like assignments.js).
//
// Each question:
//   { id, lectures: ['03', ...], type: 'compute' | 'concept', q:{en,ru}, a:{en,ru}, work?:[...] }
//   - lectures: course.json lecture ids ('01'..'08') — drives the filter chips AND the
//     "where to revise" deep-links into /book/<id>. Multiple ids = a cross-cutting topic.
//   - type: 'compute' = a by-hand calculation (🖊, the course's signature skill);
//           'concept' = explain / contrast / why (💡).
//   - a: the worked answer revealed on click (detailed — a study key, not just a nudge).
//   - work: OPTIONAL language-neutral, monospace "paper math" — the by-hand computation
//           on a toy input (a merge ledger, a BM25/nDCG/RRF run, a one-hot/BoW vector,
//           an attention/MaxSim pass, a training objective written out and evaluated).
//           Required for every 'compute' question; allowed on a 'concept' one when a
//           little table or formula sheet helps. Rendered verbatim in a <pre> block.

